From: Andre Watson <dre@ligandal.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:19:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/32] perf(moe): 4-launch expert-centric small-batch NVFP4
 MoE for T<=16 (SGLANG_QWENOPT_FUSE_SBMOE)

Replaces flashinfer cutlass_fused_moe (9 launches: 3 prefix sums, expand, strides, GEMM1, act,
GEMM2, finalize) for NVFP4 MoE calls with T<=16 by: input quant, expert-centric fc1+SwiGLU+fp4 quant
(weights decoded once per expert via cvt.rn.f16x2.e2m1x2, tensor-core dot over all routed tokens),
expert-centric fc2, top-k-ordered fp32 finalize. Same quant recipes and accumulation structure.
Tests (GPU2, real layers 20 and 5, real router on real-token rows, sglang _run_flashinfer_cutlass
path): output BITWISE equal to stock at T=1,2,4,8,16 (~42 windows each), CUDA-graph replay with
changing inputs == eager stock, deterministic. us/call off->on (20 rotating inputs): layer 20 T=1
60.0->35.4, T=4 137.0->112.7, T=16 260.1->234.6; 188-SM emulation T=4 90.7->63.8.
Off by default; eligibility-gated (fp4, bf16 in/out, tp=ep=1, plain SwiGLU, shapes); else stock.
